      <workList xml:id="workDesc_f4107529">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e222219">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_745be8fd">A2:008</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_e9eb8f33" xml:lang="it">Symphonia a 6</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_ced866a7">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_b3e85c3b">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_bf3f620f">
               <p xml:id="idm165">The 'Symphonia a 6' is one of several works found in the Fürstlich zu Bentheim-Tecklenburgische Musikbibliothek (see also SchW A1:009, A1:010, A2:004, A2:009). <persName xml:id="idm166" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Count Moritz Casimir I</persName>, who reigned 1710–68, played both the flute and cello in the daily court concerts which took place before dinner ('Tafel'). It is listed in the music library's thematic catalogue which was begun by <persName xml:id="idm167" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johann Martin Doemming</persName> in November 1750 and hence the work must have been acquired before that date – perhaps through a contact to the collegium musicum in Leipzig. The collection also includes manuscripts of works by <persName xml:id="idm168" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Georg Philipp Telemann</persName>, the <persName xml:id="idm169" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Graun</persName> brothers (Carl Heinrich and Johann Gottlieb) and <persName xml:id="idm170" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johan Joachim Agrell</persName>, among others. As the title mentions 'Scheibe in Copenhagen', it is also possible that the transcript was acquired directly from Scheibe after his employment as Kapellmeister at the Danish court in 1740. The work might be an early work and among those mention in his autobiography (Mattheson's, <rend xml:id="idm171" fontstyle="italic">Grundlage, </rend>1740; SchW C5:001).</p>
            </history>
